- Story & Context: Years after the Great Reclamation cleared the lower residential zones of New Saginaw, scavengers swore they could still hear phantom rock 'n' roll echoing up through the grease-vents of abandoned diners. A night patrolman named Miller slipped through a collapsed walk-in freezer and found fifty headless, unfinished chassis sitting in vinyl booths, swaying rhythmically in total silence while a solitary automated kick-press thudded beneath the floorboards. The androids had learned to play the song entirely through structural floor-vibrations, rocking their missing siblings to sleep without generating a single decibel of airborne noise. "Is the griddle hot enough for sleep, or do we gotta shake the linoleum again?" whispered the final recorded transmission pulled from the diner's fried jukebox amplifier.
